title: Drag and drop
intro: Things the player picks up with the mouse, and places to drop them that take only the right kind, snap them into place and say when every one is filled. No code.
project: Empty | Gem Sorter

chapter: Gems and holes | A Draggable and a Drop Target
create: Sprite
rename: Red Hole
set: Transform.Position.X = 3
set: Transform.Position.Y = 1.5
set: Sprite.Size = 1.4, 1.4
set: Sprite.Tint = #5A2A2A
add: DropTarget
set: DropTarget.Accepts = Red
set: DropTarget.AllFullMessage = Solved
explain: component:DropTarget | Drop Target | A Drop Target is a place to drop things: a hole a piece fits, a card's place on the table, an inventory slot.
explain: field:DropTarget.Accepts | Accepts | It takes only the kinds named here, so this hole takes red gems and nothing else.
explain: field:DropTarget.Capacity | Capacity, Snap and Swap | It holds one at a time, pulls what lands on it into its middle, and with Swap, dropping on a full slot swaps the two, as in an inventory.
deselect
create: Sprite
rename: Blue Hole
set: Transform.Position.X = 3
set: Transform.Position.Y = -1.5
set: Sprite.Size = 1.4, 1.4
set: Sprite.Tint = #2A2A5A
add: DropTarget
set: DropTarget.Accepts = Blue
set: DropTarget.AllFullMessage = Solved
say: A blue hole below it, with the same All Full Message.
deselect
create: Sprite
rename: Red Gem
set: Transform.Position.X = -4
set: Transform.Position.Y = 1.5
set: Sprite.Tint = #E04848
set: Sprite.Order = 2
add: Draggable
set: Draggable.Kind = Red
set: Draggable.OnlyOnTargets = true
explain: component:Draggable | Draggable | A Draggable is something the player picks up with the mouse: press on it, carry it, let go.
explain: field:Draggable.Kind | Kind | Its kind is what the holes check.
explain: field:Draggable.OnlyOnTargets | Only On Targets | And with this ticked, let go anywhere but a hole that takes it, it slides back where it came from.
deselect
create: Sprite
rename: Blue Gem
set: Transform.Position.X = -4
set: Transform.Position.Y = -1.5
set: Sprite.Tint = #4870E0
set: Sprite.Order = 2
add: Draggable
set: Draggable.Kind = Blue
set: Draggable.OnlyOnTargets = true
say: And a blue gem.
deselect
create: Text
rename: Solved
set: Transform.Position.Y = 3.5
add: Counter
set: Counter.Message = Solved
set: Counter.Format = Solved: {0}
say: Last, a counter that counts the Solved message, so we can see it arrive.

chapter: Sorting them | Wrong holes turn gems away
play
wait: 0.5
gamedrag: Red Gem > Blue Hole
wait: 0.5
expectat: Red Gem = -4, 1.5
explain: game | Turned away | The blue hole doesn't take red gems, so it slides back.
gamedrag: Red Gem > Red Hole + 0.3, 0.3
wait: 0.5
expectat: Red Gem = 3, 1.5
say: Dropped near the red hole's middle, it snaps right into it.
gamedrag: Blue Gem > Blue Hole
wait: 0.5
expectat: Blue Gem = 3, -1.5
explain: game | Solved | Both holes are full now, so they send their All Full Message, once, and the counter shows it. Holes also send a message when something lands on them or is taken off, and gems when they're picked up and let go.
stop
say: That's drag and drop with the mouse: cards, jigsaw pieces, inventories and sorting puzzles, with no code. Things can snap to a grid off the targets too, and in a network game each player drags with their own mouse.
